  <!-- ============ FEATURES ============ -->
  <section id="features" aria-labelledby="features-h">
    <h2 id="features-h">Features</h2>
    <ul class="features">
      <li><b>Three reverb engines</b><ul class="sub3">
        <li><b>Dark FDN 1 (Sub):</b> a feedback delay network built for low end, tuned to keep the kick's fundamental punch.</li>
        <li><b>Dark FDN 2 (Texture):</b> the same network, larger and fully diffused, with slow, constant modulation: a bright, moving wash.</li>
        <li><b>Mutable:</b> the plate reverb from Mutable Instruments' Rings, open source.</li></ul></li>
      <li><b>Staged Drive</b><span>Saturation in three types, chosen on the switch. Drive grips the band above 90 Hz first, so the sub stays clean; the last quarter of the knob brings the sub in too, for a fully driven rumble.</span></li>
      <li><b>Split: rumble and texture, two outputs</b><span>A crossover from 40 Hz to 2 kHz, about 120 Hz at noon. Everything below it goes to Out 1 as rumble; everything above goes to Out 2 as texture. Both are ducked, and the two add back up to the whole sound.</span></li>
      <li><b>Predelay and Feedback</b><span>Up to 666 ms of predelay pushes the swell off the kick. Turn up Feedback and the delay repeats, each repeat re-triggering the reverb, so the swells stack into a rolling rumble. Even at full, the repeats fade out on their own.</span></li>
      <li><b>Built-in sidechain ducking</b><span>Fired by a gate, or detected from the kick itself. The rumble on Out 1 drops out completely on every hit, so the kick has the low end to itself; the texture on Out 2 isn't ducked. With a gate, its length sets how long the rumble stays down, and Release sets how long it takes to swell back, as a share of that length, so a sequencer reshapes every duck. The Hold knob sets how long it stays down with no gate, and stretches or shortens every gate's hold with one.</span></li>
      <li><b>Mix In</b><span>Noise or any other source joins after Drive, just before the split. It skips the reverb and Drive, so it stays clean. Most of it lands on Out 2, where it plays straight through; the part below the split pumps with the rumble.</span></li>
      <li><b>Automatic input level</b><span>Quiet and hot kicks drive the rumble the same way. No input gain to set.</span></li>
      <li><b>Hot outputs</b><span>Both outputs run near full level, with a soft clipper as a safety net. Set the level at your mixer or an attenuator. For the dry kick, take it from a stackcable or mult before the input.</span></li>
      <li><b>CV for every knob</b><span>Seven CV inputs, one per knob, for per-step modulation. Four lights show the trigger source, the gate, the rumble level and the predelay repeats.</span></li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <!-- ============ LISTEN ============ -->
  <section id="listen" aria-labelledby="listen-h">
    <h2 id="listen-h">Listen</h2>
    <p>Each loop plays in three versions that stay in sync: the <span class="k">kick</span> alone, the <span class="r">rumble</span> alone, and the two mixed. Switch between them while it plays to hear what Shindo Versio adds.</p>
    <div class="presets">
      <div class="preset"><b>Rolling</b><span class="d">Mutable plate, predelay repeats stacked with Feedback.</span><div class="seg" role="group" aria-label="Rolling: version"><button disabled>Kick</button><button disabled>Rumble</button><button disabled>Mix</button></div></div>
      <div class="preset"><b>Deep</b><span class="d">Dark FDN 1, Out 1, Split low: a sub that breathes with the kick.</span><div class="seg" role="group" aria-label="Deep: version"><button disabled>Kick</button><button disabled>Rumble</button><button disabled>Mix</button></div></div>
      <div class="preset"><b>Texture</b><span class="d">Dark FDN 2, Out 2: a moving mid-range wash.</span><div class="seg" role="group" aria-label="Texture: version"><button disabled>Kick</button><button disabled>Rumble</button><button disabled>Mix</button></div></div>
      <div class="preset"><b>Triplet</b><span class="d">Predelay on a dotted eighth: repeats drift 3 against 4.</span><div class="seg" role="group" aria-label="Triplet: version"><button disabled>Kick</button><button disabled>Rumble</button><button disabled>Mix</button></div></div>
    </div>
    <p class="note"><span class="todo">Coming</span> The recordings are made once the sound is final, from the same engine that runs on the module.</p>
  </section>

