    <p>The kick goes two ways: to the detector, and into the rumble path: predelay (with its feedback loop), smear and drive. Mix In joins after Drive. Then Split divides the sound: below it goes to <b>Out 1</b> as rumble, above it to <b>Out 2</b> as texture. The duck is fired by a patched gate, or by the detector when there is none. It pulls Out 1 all the way down on each trigger, with an attack, a hold (the gate's length, or the Hold knob with no gate) and a swelling release. Out 2 isn't ducked.</p>
